      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:8:8:5",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ الرِّضَا ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ الرِّيشِ أَ ذَكِيٌّ هُوَ فَقَالَ كَانَ أَبِي ( عليه السلام ) يَتَوَسَّدُ الرِّيشَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Muhammad Bin Bundar, from Ahmad Bin Abu Abdullah, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Abu Nasr, from Abu Jareer Al Qummy who said, ",
          "‘I asked Al-Reza<sup>asws</sup> about the feather, is it pure?’ So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘My<sup>asws</sup> father<sup>asws</sup> used to stuff the pillow with the feathers’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Bandar has narrated from Ahmad ibn abu ‘Abd Allah from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from ibn abu Nasr from abu Jarir al-Qummiy who has said the following: “I once asked al-Rida’, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about feathers; if it is lawful. He (the Imam) said, ‘My father would use a pillow of feathers.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
